### 🐍 Python Strings – The "Exam Ready" Cheat Sheet

#### 1. The Golden Rule (Memorize this!)
> **Python strings are IMMUTABLE.**
> *This means:* `str.replace()` or `str.upper()` **does NOT change** the original string. It creates a **brand new string**. 
> *Contrast with Java:* Java `String` is also Immutable. Python does **NOT** have a `StringBuffer` or `StringBuilder` equivalent built into the core language (you'd have to use lists).

---

#### 2. The "Gotcha" Methods (Most MCQ Traps)

| Method | The Trick to Remember | Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`len()`** | It's a **FUNCTION** (not a method like Java's `.length()`). You write `len(str)`, not `str.len()`. | `len("Hi")` → `2` |
| **`find()`** | Returns **`-1`** if not found. (Java returns `-1` too; C++ returns `npos`). | `"Hi".find('z')` → `-1` |
| **`split()`** | Returns a **LIST** (array) of strings. | `"a,b".split(',')` → `['a','b']` |
| **`join()`** | The **delimiter comes FIRST!** It's `"-".join(list)`, NOT `list.join("-")`. | `"-".join(["1","2"])` → `"1-2"` |
| **`replace()`** | Replaces **ALL** occurrences unless you specify a count. | `"aaa".replace('a','b')` → `"bbb"` |
| **`strip()`** | Removes ONLY leading/trailing spaces. Does NOT remove middle spaces. | `" Hi ".strip()` → `"Hi"` |

---

#### 3. Case Conversion (Quick Reference)

| Method | What it does | Input → Output |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `str.upper()` | ALL CAPS | `"Hi"` → `"HI"` |
| `str.lower()` | all lowercase | `"HI"` → `"hi"` |
| `str.capitalize()` | **First** letter capital, rest lower | `"hi WORLD"` → `"Hi world"` |
| `str.title()` | **Every word** capital, rest lower | `"hi WORLD"` → `"Hi World"` |

